= The January Rising

On 4 January the government dismissed Emil Eichhorn, the Independent who ran the Berlin police. The next day a vast crowd marched in protest, and armed men occupied *Vorwärts* and the other papers of the newspaper district. A Revolutionary Committee of the shop stewards, the Independents and our party declared Ebert deposed. Karl Liebknecht signed for us without asking the Zentrale.

Rosa Luxemburg thinks the rising cannot win: the provinces are quiet and the garrison will not march. But the buildings are held, and the men inside want to know what for.

- @overthrow: Back the Committee: Ebert must go.
- @occupations: Hold the buildings, but call for no insurrection.
- @negotiate: Ask the Independents to mediate.

@overthrow
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The occupiers will fight harder, and Noske gets his excuse sooner.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids an uprising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.jan_line = 1;
Q.e19_arms += 1;
Q.e19_noske += 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.district_berlin_loyalty += 8;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Noske\'s volunteers: 3,000, at Dahlem';
!}

*Die Rote Fahne* calls on the workers of Berlin to finish the work of November.

@occupations
subtitle: Luxemburg's line. The fighters will ask what they are holding the buildings for.
on-arrival: jan_line = 2; lean_luxemburgist += 2; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4

The party demands Eichhorn's return and the arming of the workers. It does not call for the government's fall.

@negotiate
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Liebknecht leaves the Committee. Berlin's workers will call it desertion.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids negotiating with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.jan_line = 3;
Q.e19_talks = 1;
Q.e19_lieb_committee = 0;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.district_berlin_loyalty -= 10;
!}

Kautsky and Breitscheid agree to go between the Chancellery and the Committee. In the *Vorwärts* building, some of the men tear up our leaflet.
